# nearby.suite — nearby on a simulated LAN: an unowned node listed and admitted
# by its nearby alias, two nodes of one User meeting in stealth, a Silent node
# sending nothing, a sibling relinked the moment it is heard again, and a
# fresh node joining a Stealth node with user.join alone; and, off the default
# listen ports, an unowned node admitted and two fresh Stealth nodes of one User
# linking through the ports their statuses carry.
#
# Every test runs VM operations: nearby needs a LAN, and a local world has
# none (ether skips loopback). The first four continue the one before, so they
# are one chain in one simulation, and a failure skips the tests after it. The
# order puts the long outage last. nearby-join claims the reflector, which
# nearby-stealth-meet needs unowned, so it runs in a world of its own that
# replays nearby-adopt. The two -ports tests move nodes off tcp 1791 and kcp
# 1792, a node config no other test shares, so each runs in a world of its
# own.
nearby-adopt
nearby-stealth-meet
nearby-silent
nearby-relink
nearby-join
nearby-adopt-ports
nearby-stealth-meet-ports
